<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I7df5242dade936ae2236a882e62ddabd8c5923ba" commit="92da282258881aa8cb0fccce389b50f463b4c0b7" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ARM: rockchip: Handle ERRATA 821420 for resume  The normal prov-v7.S code doesn't run on the main CPU during resume from S3.  Apply the errata early in the resume at the same time that we restore the l2ctlr.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47192 TEST=kernel_CheckArmErrata autotest  Change-Id: I7df5242dade936ae2236a882e62ddabd8c5923ba Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331745 Reviewed-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331745" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/45/331745/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I54f02bc7e2af5e071cad83c85049737a9c5cd86a" commit="d78495586360473d6a14341acce88e379428a39f" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: Turn on CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_821420  This errata affects rk3288 and we care about that.  Enable it.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47192 TEST=kernel_CheckArmErrata autotest  Change-Id: I54f02bc7e2af5e071cad83c85049737a9c5cd86a Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331746 Reviewed-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331746" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/46/331746/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ib0add104a5cf5cd8875bc5dc2c0f82c2657f6984" commit="5cca809466452be16243eb5833236cc1246240b8" commit_message="drm/nouveau/fb: add comptagline's granularity for Tegra GPUs  On Kepler and Maxwell one comptagline can cover one 128KB page. If the 64KB large page is used, one comptagline covers two large pages. This patch allocates the comptagline according to the comptagline's granularity and avoids leak of comptags backing storage.  Change-Id: Ib0add104a5cf5cd8875bc5dc2c0f82c2657f6984 Signed-off-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331471 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Konsta Holtta &lt;kholtta@nvidia.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331471" owner_email="vince.h@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/71/331471/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I13373a9ef2b7fec750573a9d4502f3619f6758b3" commit="9cb5878e6de0a29a2133d268e54c06c9cf7f9f44" commit_message="drm/nouveau/instmem: program tag info with more considerations  Previously we used one tagline for one large page, that worked for 128KB page but wasted tags for 64KB page, so now the comptagline granularity and large page size have to be taken into account when programming tag in PTE, and one comptagline can cover one 128KB page or two 64K pages correctly.  Given two 64K pages which have non-contiguous virtual address might share the same comptagline, which is happening with Vulkan apps, we have to enable USE_FULL_COMP_TAG_LINE. And we set the MSB of comptag index to indicate the PTE is referring to the bottom half of a comptag. Below is an example for that. We keep a 1:1 mapping of physical address to comptagline (and half) no matter where in virtual address space we map it.  GVA         PA          COMPTAG_INDEX ----------  ----------  ------------- 0x00010000  0xC0010000  0x00000 0x00080000  0xC0020000  0x10000 0x00020000  0xC0030000  0x00001 0x00070000  0xC0040000  0x10001  Change-Id: I13373a9ef2b7fec750573a9d4502f3619f6758b3 Signed-off-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331473 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Konsta Holtta &lt;kholtta@nvidia.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331473" owner_email="vince.h@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/73/331473/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I33fea84f32269fc6eaff2080823d124f5bc0785d" commit="77871f7d3cb0e93b2f952374a95c3fd61df3d481" commit_message="Add Elm builder to Oak group  BUG=chromium:591300 TEST=None  Change-Id: I33fea84f32269fc6eaff2080823d124f5bc0785d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329956 Commit-Ready: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Paris Yeh &lt;pyeh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329956" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/56/329956/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9085d87f00d0c5ad6df1cc733764329f9c41816e" commit="8816a611254110da5cc5bf04981af59a304a3842" commit_message="Add new devices  BUG=chromium:None TEST=None  Change-Id: I9085d87f00d0c5ad6df1cc733764329f9c41816e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330213 Commit-Ready: Tien Chang &lt;tienchang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Tien Chang &lt;tienchang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aashutosh Kalyankar &lt;aashutoshk@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tien Chang &lt;tienchang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aashutosh Kalyankar &lt;aashutoshk@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="330213" owner_email="aashutoshk@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/crostestutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crostestutils" ref="refs/changes/13/330213/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I275744f3661d31edff7b33dbeec90f6d17d34281" commit="cbbf3188ad554283a5d2f314a9962e7499638140" commit_message="net-print/cups-filters: upgraded package to upstream  Upgraded net-print/cups-filters to version 1.8.2 on amd64, arm, x86  This brings in the USE=postscript support I submitted. Pulled in with &quot;--unstable-ok&quot;. The only real use cases are still in development, so this shouldn't be a risk.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47758,chrome-os-partner:49267 TEST=`USE=&quot;-postscript -foomatic&quot; emerge-${BOARD} cups-filters`; check that      &quot;gstoxxx&quot; and &quot;foomatic-rip&quot; filters are missing TEST=print some test pages  Change-Id: I275744f3661d31edff7b33dbeec90f6d17d34281 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/327210 Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="327210" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable" ref="refs/changes/10/327210/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iae2b87f1a2dc20891bd298128097f1d4d7f27bf6" commit="cb2d04ced0c003554a175199ece7c17ae999e0ca" commit_message="[Autotest] touch_MouseScroll to use actual scrolling again.  Instead of counting from the mouse wheel events, physically scroll the page (as is done in touch_TouchscreenScroll).  This is because on link and samus, the one value is 2x the other. It doesn't matter for touch_ScrollDirection, which checkes only the direction of the scroll.  It /does/ matter for this test, which checks the absolute value of the delta for a single mouse click.  TEST=ran on link, samus, and others BUG=None  Change-Id: Iae2b87f1a2dc20891bd298128097f1d4d7f27bf6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331774 Commit-Ready: Katherine Threlkeld &lt;kathrelkeld@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Katherine Threlkeld &lt;kathrelkeld@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: danny chan &lt;dchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331774" owner_email="kathrelkeld@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/74/331774/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I1ccec2ee90fa925ea36dcba42b8f6f51da824eef" commit="db964ac3a034daefb56a141fdbaa149068aa457c" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mfd: cros_ec_lpc: Fix build as module  MFD_CROS_EC_LPC can be configured as module. Doing so results in the followong build errors.  ERROR: &quot;cros_ec_lpc_reg_destroy&quot; [drivers/platform/chrome/cros_ec_lpc.ko] undefined! ERROR: &quot;cros_ec_lpc_write_bytes&quot; [drivers/platform/chrome/cros_ec_lpc.ko] undefined! ERROR: &quot;cros_ec_lpc_read_bytes&quot; [drivers/platform/chrome/cros_ec_lpc.ko] undefined!  This happens because the Makefile actually treats cros_ec_lpc.o and cros_ec_lpc_reg.o as separate modules. The functions are defined in cros_ec_lpc_reg.o and not exported.  Since it does not add any value to have those two files as separate modules, define a combined module which includes both files.  BUG=chromium:583462 TEST=Build x86_64:allmodconfig  Change-Id: I1ccec2ee90fa925ea36dcba42b8f6f51da824eef Fixes: 95faf7ae0844 (&quot;CHROMIUM: cros_ec_lpc: Add support for mec1322 EC&quot;) Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332033 Reviewed-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332033" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/33/332033/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ie4621168c424be2a3aa501b96beb57a374daeb80" commit="cbc77b1c7a89deb12cf2766400e15a8574de6999" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Input: elants_i2c - wire up regulator support  Elan touchscreen controllers use two power supplies, vcc33 and vccio, and we need to enable them before trying to access the device. On X86 firmware usually does this, but on ARM it is usually left to the kernel.  Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Scott Liu &lt;scott.liu@emc.com.tw&gt; Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dmitry.torokhov@gmail.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit afe10358e47a3ea1f69005cb1be78170d23f8afa) Signed-off-by: YH Huang &lt;yh.huang@mediatek.com&gt;  BUG=none TEST=build pass and touchscreen works fine on oak-rev5  Change-Id: Ie4621168c424be2a3aa501b96beb57a374daeb80 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331520 Commit-Ready: YH Huang &lt;yh.huang@mediatek.com&gt; Tested-by: YH Huang &lt;yh.huang@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331520" owner_email="yh.huang@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/20/331520/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib77c9199e210dd615ddd41f649165e780b402071" commit="b25f4e4a68966aea96a92e31e166db35f411745c" commit_message="Explicitly 